SWEET HFS mount trace for USB-root probe 5 (patch 0171), opt-in: boot-arg sweethfstrace=N (N > 0; absent or 0 = off, nothing printed). Lines start with "SWEET HFSTRACE: [<ms since boot> ms]". HFS side (bsd/sweet_hfs/core, staged by 0026): hfs_mountfs enter/return (both exits), hfs_MountHFSPlusVolume enter/return at both call sites with elapsed ms, async bitmap scan thread create/registered and in the thread start/bitmap lock taken/ScanUnmapBlocks returned/returns, the synchronous scan branch, the hotfile interlock wait for the scan and hfs_recording_init enter/return (mount and rw-upgrade call sites). usbroot side (bsd/dev/sweet_usbroot.c, needs 0157/0158): the first N reads reaching ur_strategy with block, byte offset, size, host fills, ur_lock wait, total ms, thread id and error; N is capped at 4096 (loud clamp line) and the cap hit is logged. Read-only: printf only, no register access, no disk write, no change to any HFS decision. Clean room (idea only from research 97 5b.1). Not compiled yet (tools/xnu-local-build, AP-147) and not run on hardware.
